38
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,700
Depolarization is the rising phase.

39
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:19,480
Voltage gated sodium channels open and sodium ions

40
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:22,840
rush in down, the electrochemical gradient.

41
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,360
The inside rapidly becomes less negative.

42
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,240
Then positive.

43
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,860
The membrane is now depolarized.

44
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:36,020
On the graph, this is the steep upstroke from threshold

45
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:36,720
to the peak.

46
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,560
At the peak, two things change.

47
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:44,740
The voltage gated sodium channels become inactivated.

48
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:48,640
Inactivation is not the same as simply closing.

49
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:53,340
A part of the protein blocks, the open pore from the inside.

50
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:57,820
So sodium entry stops, even though the membrane is still positive.

51
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,720
At the same time, voltage gated potassium channels

52
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,180
opened.

53
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:07,220
They are slower to open than the sodium channels.

54
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:12,060
Repolarization is the falling phase.

55
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:15,720
Potassium ions leave the axon through

56
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,080
those open voltage gated potassium channels.

57
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:19,880
BAN!

58
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:21,860
Positive charge leaves.

59
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:25,100
So the inside becomes negative again.

60
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:30,180
This rapid fall is caused by potassium efflux

61
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,460
and sodium inactivation.

62
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,560
It's not caused by the sodium.

63
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,440
Potassium pump.

64
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:40,220
The pump is far too slow to

65
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,480
produce this millisecond downstroke.

66
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:45,340
I'm with an anti -spiral.

67
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:50,460
The pump's job is to restore the ion gradients afterward.

68
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:54,900
The membrane often goes a little more negative than rest.

69
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,320
That, on the shoot, is hyperpolarization, sometimes called

70
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,260
